{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the word הואלתי is not [a standard form].</b> Like החילותי, except its meaning is 'I desired.' And thus 'הואיל משה' (Deuteronomy 1:5). The kaf of אנכי is superfluous, or they are two words and the meaning is one." "And the sense of 'I am dust and ash' is: dust I was and ash I shall return to, the principle referring to the foundation of the body, which is the bones:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:59.982960901Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}